# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers, so their line endings are not a
# matter of local preference.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true - the Windows default, and this project expects Windows
# developers - a checkout rewrote every .sh to CRLF. `COPY . /app` then baked
# that into the image, and `#!/usr/bin/env bash` became `bash\r`:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which restart-loops the api container with an error that says nothing about
# line endings. The files are LF in the index; this keeps them LF on disk too.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Reference data that must never be touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls binary
*.docx binary
*.msg binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
